  "id": "chromeclinic",
  "note": "A CHAMFERED tower, built out of two boxes rather than a drum: a square core with a second square inside it turned 45 degrees and set to about 0.85 of its width, so the union reads as an eight-sided shaft. The trick is worth knowing because it is the only way to get a faceted tower in this format that still LIGHTS ITSELF — an authored drum is drawn as a flat palette shade with no night term (drawAuthoredModel builds its skin from the palette RGB and the face normal and nothing else) and carries no mountable wall, where a box keeps its texture, its lit windows and the whole derivedTrim kit. The drum is kept only for the cap, where there is nothing to light. ⚠ The two cores are COINCIDENT mass and are deliberately not the same width: equal squares at 45 degrees give an eight-pointed star, not an octagon. RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms puts the asc_clinic arm back.",
